---
description: Enforce Larrick branch-domain ownership and branch naming.
alwaysApply: true
---

These rules **add stricter git conventions** when the in-repo Cursor plugin ([`larrick-worktree-workflow`](../)) is **enabled**. They do **not** replace the baseline workflow in [`Larrick_multi/AGENTS.md`](../../../AGENTS.md): outside this plugin, `main` remains the documented branch and there is no required branch naming scheme unless your team adopts this plugin.

- Use `codex/<workflow>/<short-topic>` branch naming for task branches.
- Land changes on owning `dev/<workflow>` first, then promote to `main`.
- Do not propose edits outside the owning domain paths unless explicitly requested.
- Do not push directly to `main` or any `dev/*` branch.
